//! The TPS55288 buck-boost converter with an I2C interface, Texas Instruments, in the 26-pin
//! VQFN-HR package (RPM, 3.5 x 4 mm, 0.5 mm pitch), order code TPS55288RPMR: the U3 of the Power
//! Manifold charger module (the board's footprint is `Local Library:VQFN-HR-26_L4.0-W3.5_
//! TPS55288RPMR` and the LCSC number it carries, C2864583, is the TPS55288RPMR).
//!
//! The pin table was WRITTEN BY HAND from TI's datasheet "TPS55288 36-V, 16-A Buck-boost
//! Converter with I2C Interface" (literature number SLVSF01B, November 2018, revised December
//! 2020, 55 pages in the PDF TI serves, fetched on 2026-11-11 from
//! <https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps55288.pdf>, SHA-256 `2b60a3054038`): section 5, Figure 5-1
//! "26-pin VQFN-HR, RPM Package (Transparent Top View)" and Table 5-1 "Pin Functions" (printed
//! pages 3 and 4) for the pad numbers, names, I/O types and descriptions. The datasheet is
//! copyrighted (Texas Instruments): only facts are taken here (numbers, names, kinds).
//!
//! The package has 26 pins: 23 on the edge, numbered as the figure counts them (1 to 7 down the
//! left, 8 to 13 along the bottom, 14 to 19 up the right and 20 to 23 along the top), and three
//! at the middle of the underside, 24 `PGND`, 25 `SW2` and 26 `VOUT`, which the table gives
//! as the second pad of each of those three pins (`PGND` is "9, 24", `SW2` "21, 25" and `VOUT`
//! "11, 26"). The pins with two pads are one pin each here.
//!
//! The kinds follow Table 5-1's I/O column: `PWR` (`VIN`, `PGND`, `AGND`, `VOUT`) is `power`;
//! `I` (`EN/UVLO`, `SCL`, `DITH/SYNC`, `MODE`, `COMP`, `ISP`, `ISN`) is `input`; `O` (`DR1L`,
//! `DR1H`, `FSW`, `CDC`, `ILIM`, `VCC`) is `output`; `I/O` (`SDA`, `FB/INT`) is
//! `bidirectional`. Four pins are written otherwise on purpose. `SW1` and `SW2` are the
//! switching nodes of the two half bridges, between the inductor and the power switches, and
//! `BOOT1` and `BOOT2` are the bootstrap capacitors' pins: the table prints `I` for `SW1`,
//! `SW2` and `BOOT1`, and `O` for `BOOT2`, but none of them is a signal the part reads or
//! drives (the descriptions say a node of the power stage and a capacitor to it), so all four
//! are `passive`, as the inductor pins of the TPS63802 part are. `COMP` is printed `I` and
//! described as "output of the internal error amplifier. Connect the loop compensation network
//! between this pin and AGND": it is `input` as the table's column has it, and a board that
//! joins only a network to it will meet the rule that an input must be driven.
//!
//! The input is a rail, `.vin`: `.vin.pos` is `VIN` and `.vin.neg` is `PGND` (pads 9 and 24),
//! with the datasheet's recommended input voltage, section 6.3 "Recommended Operating
//! Conditions" (printed page 5): VIN 2.7 V minimum and 36 V maximum. `AGND` (pad 10) is a
//! pin of its own: the datasheet calls it the signal ground and does not say the two grounds are one net (the
//! reference board joins them), so the part does not join them.
//!
//! The output is a rail too, `.vout`: `.vout.pos` is `VOUT` (pads 11 and 26) and `.vout.neg` is
//! `PGND`, joined to the input's inside the part (the datasheet's one power ground), with the
//! recommended output voltage of section 6.3 (printed page 5): 0.8 V minimum and 22 V maximum.
//!
//! At DC the part is a switching regulator (`dc switching_regulator`, ADR 0076, amendment 3):
//! its output rail is an ideal source over the board's output voltage and its input draws
//! `Pout / (efficiency * Vin)` and its quiescent current. The statement assumes no topology (a
//! power balance), so it is right for a buck-boost as for a buck. Its numbers:
//!
//! - The efficiency has no figure in any table of the datasheet; it is read by eye off the
//!   curves of section 6.7, Typical Characteristics, Figures 6-1 to 6-10 "Efficiency vs Output
//!   Current" (printed pages 10 and 11: VOUT 5 V, 9 V, 12 V, 15 V and 20 V, each in FPWM and in
//!   PFM, each with VIN 5 V, 9 V, 12 V and 20 V, at TA 25 C and fSW 400 kHz, the frequency this
//!   board's 49.9 kohm sets). Over output currents from 0.5 A to 10 A every curve lies between
//!   about 81 % (Figure 6-5, VOUT 12 V, VIN 5 V, FPWM, at 10 A) and about 98 % (Figures 6-3 and
//!   6-5 near 2 A), so the default is `0.80..0.98`, rounded outward. Below 0.5 A the efficiency
//!   falls (to about 30 % at 10 mA in FPWM, Figure 6-1): a board that runs there, or at another
//!   frequency, states its own from the figures.
//! - The quiescent current into VIN is 860 uA at most, 760 uA typical (section 6.5, Electrical
//!   Characteristics, printed page 6: IC enabled, no load, no switching, VIN 3 V to 24 V, TJ up
//!   to 125 C). The default is `0A..860uA`: a maximum and no minimum. Above 24 V the datasheet
//!   gives no figure, so a board that runs its input there states its own.
//!
//! What is deliberately left out: the absolute maximum ratings (Section 6.1: VIN and SW1 40 V;
//! VOUT, SW2, ISP and ISN 25 V; EN 20 V; the signal pins 6 V), the inductance and capacitance
//! ranges, the current limit, the reference voltage, the internal switches' resistance and every
//! register of the I2C interface. No std generic is a buck-boost converter (`Buck`'s doc in
//! `std/parts/regulator.nsm` says why), so the part provides none. The external half bridge on
//! `DR1H` and `DR1L` (the board's Q1 and Q2) carries the input power on this board, and is not
//! part of this model.
import std::sources::Rail

/// The TPS55288 in the 26-pin VQFN-HR package: a synchronous four-switch buck-boost converter
/// with an I2C interface, 2.7 V to 36 V in and 0.8 V to 22 V out. The pin names are the
/// datasheet's (Table 5-1's `DR1H`, which section 6.1 writes `DRH1`)
/// and the pad numbers its pin numbers. `.vin` is the input rail: `.vin.pos` the `VIN` pad and
/// `.vin.neg` the `PGND` pads; `.vout` the output rail, `.vout.pos` the `VOUT` pads, with the
/// same ground. At DC it is a switching regulator (see the file's doc for its numbers).
part Tps55288 {
    .designator &= "U"

    .vin: Rail
    // Section 6.3, Recommended Operating Conditions (printed page 5): VIN 2.7 V to 36 V.
    .vin.voltage >= 2.7V
    .vin.voltage <= 36V

    .vout: Rail
    .vout.neg ~ .vin.neg
    // Section 6.3, Recommended Operating Conditions (printed page 5): VOUT 0.8 V to 22 V.
    .vout.voltage >= 0.8V
    .vout.voltage <= 22V

    /// The efficiency, a fraction: read off Figures 6-1 to 6-10 (section 6.7, printed pages 10
    /// and 11) over output currents from 0.5 A to 10 A, the lowest point Figure 6-5 (VOUT 12 V,
    /// VIN 5 V, FPWM, 10 A, about 81 %), rounded outward. A board that runs at a lighter load or
    /// another frequency states its own from the figures.
    .efficiency: Number
    .efficiency ?= 0.80..0.98

    /// The current the IC draws into VIN for itself: 860 uA at most (section 6.5, Electrical
    /// Characteristics, printed page 6, "Quiescent current into the VIN pin", IC enabled, no
    /// load, no switching, VIN 3 V to 24 V, TJ up to 125 C). A maximum and no minimum.
    .quiescent_current: Current
    .quiescent_current ?= 0A..860uA

    // What the input draws: what the output supplies over the efficiency, and the IC's own.
    .vin.current == -.vout.current * .vout.voltage / (.vin.voltage * .efficiency) + .quiescent_current
    dc switching_regulator .vin .vout .efficiency .quiescent_current

    pins "VQFN-26-HR(3.5x4)" {
        //  pin       kind           name         pads
        .dr1l     output         "DR1L"       "1"
        .dr1h     output         "DR1H"       "2"
        .vin.pos  power          "VIN"        "3"
        .en       input          "EN/UVLO"    "4"
        .scl      input          "SCL"        "5"
        .sda      bidirectional  "SDA"        "6"
        .dith     input          "DITH/SYNC"  "7"
        .fsw      output         "FSW"        "8"
        .vin.neg  power          "PGND"       "9" "24"
        .agnd     power          "AGND"       "10"
        .vout.pos power          "VOUT"       "11" "26"
        .isp      input          "ISP"        "12"
        .isn      input          "ISN"        "13"
        .fb       bidirectional  "FB/INT"     "14"
        .mode     input          "MODE"       "15"
        .cdc      output         "CDC"        "16"
        .ilim     output         "ILIM"       "17"
        .comp     input          "COMP"       "18"
        .vcc      output         "VCC"        "19"
        .boot2    passive        "BOOT2"      "20"
        .sw2      passive        "SW2"        "21" "25"
        .boot1    passive        "BOOT1"      "22"
        .sw1      passive        "SW1"        "23"
    }

    .package: Package
    catalog tps55288 by .mpn { .mpn, .package }
}
